### Installation

Install virtual environment  [virtualenv](https://virtualenv.pypa.io/en/stable/installation/) for Dependency Management

```bash
pip install virtualenv
```
Create and Activate a virtual environment

```bash

virtualenv oneconsole_env

source oneconsole_env/bin/activate

```

Use the package manager [pip](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/) to install dependencies in requires.txt

```bash
pip install --upgrade -r requires/requires.txt
```
Migrate to reflect the changes made inside models.py file to database

```bash
python manage.py makemigrations

python manage.py migrate
```

Run the unittests if required
```bash
python manage.py test
```

Run the server

```bash
python manage.py runserver dafslx90:2020
```
> Note: Here Host is fixed but the Port can be changed.

Verify the deployment by navigating to your server address in your preferred browser.

```sh
dafslx90:2020
```


Host : dafslx90
Port: 2020

> Note: For Development Host is dafslx90
> For Homologation Host is hafslx90
> and for Production Host is pafslx90

### Run the Redis server

> Note: Redis should be running on background.

Activate the environment

```bash
source oneconsole_env/bin/activate
```

Activate Redis server

```bash
redis-server
```
> Do not close the terminal as it closed redis server.

### Run the Celery server

> Note: For the celery tasks to perform Asynchronous tasks,
 its should be running on background.


Activate the environment

```bash
source oneconsole_env/bin/activate
```

Move into the project

```bash
cd oneconsole
```

Run the celery server

```bash
celery -A oneconsole.celery worker -l DEBUG -E
```

> Do not close the terminal as it closed celery server.

### Create a new App

To create a new App

```sh
python manage.py startapp new_app_name
```

Add a new view named `index` inside `new_app_name/views.py`

```sh
from django.http import HttpResponse

def index(request):
    return HttpResponse("Hi customize this view_name, contents as per the requirement.")
```

Create a file  `new_app_name/urls.py`   

```sh
from django.urls import path
from . import views

urlpatterns = [
    path('', views.index, name='index'),
]
```
Include `new_app_name/urls.py`  in the root  `project_name/urls.py` file ( ie: near `settings.py` file)

```sh
from django.contrib import admin
from django.urls import include, path

urlpatterns = [
    path('new_app_name/', include('new_app_name.urls')),
    path('admin/', admin.site.urls),
]
```

Run the server

```bash
python manage.py runserver dafslx90:2020
```

